00:10:42.884 --> 00:10:45.178
with anything outside this cube,

00:10:45.178 --> 00:10:47.546
'cause I'm zoned into
the #AskGaryVee show.

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:50.634
So I'm very all in on what I'm doing,

00:10:50.634 --> 00:10:53.462
and so when I come back from that high,

00:10:53.462 --> 00:10:55.617
first of all I'm pretty
much high, although, I mean,

00:10:55.617 --> 00:10:58.608
I can create high from calm if I need it,

00:10:58.608 --> 00:11:00.442
'cause I'm hyped.

00:11:00.442 --> 00:11:01.789
And excited.

00:11:01.789 --> 00:11:03.623
Yeah, I know, I don't,

00:11:03.623 --> 00:11:05.295
this is an answer that's very difficult.

00:11:05.295 --> 00:11:06.706
I wanted to show this answer

00:11:06.706 --> 00:11:07.913
because I appreciate the question,

00:11:07.913 --> 00:11:09.841
'cause I think a lot of
people think about it.

00:11:09.841 --> 00:11:12.627
But the truth is, this
is something that comes

00:11:12.627 --> 00:11:14.758
very natural to me. It's intuitive.

00:11:14.758 --> 00:11:17.080
I would just ask all of you,
and I talk a lot about this,

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.952
I tweeted out quite a bit
over the last two weeks

00:11:19.952 --> 00:11:23.729
about my grateful kind of post on Medium.

00:11:23.729 --> 00:11:25.071
I think gratitude, Amy.

00:11:25.071 --> 00:11:27.160
I mean, just be grateful,
be grateful that you have

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.222
some down time and it's
just normal, and it's nice,

00:11:29.222 --> 00:11:31.590
and you get to see your
core friends and family,

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.021
and be very grateful
that you're lucky enough

00:11:33.021 --> 00:11:35.698
to go to five-day tech raves,

00:11:35.698 --> 00:11:38.008
where you can be on that high.

00:11:38.008 --> 00:11:40.790
- [Voiceover] Duke asks, what
would you say A.J. has learned

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.903
and applied from you in business, and,

00:11:42.903 --> 00:11:45.522
would he be willing to answer
this question on the show?

00:11:45.522 --> 00:11:46.858
- Duke, memo alert.

00:11:46.858 --> 00:11:49.065
This is the #AskGaryVee show.

00:11:49.065 --> 00:11:53.640
This is not the Ask A.J.
Vee show with no silent E's.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.723
This is my show, I answer the questions.

00:11:56.723 --> 00:11:59.811
There is no A.J. answering the questions.

00:11:59.811 --> 00:12:03.689
It's me, I do it, it's my show.

00:12:03.689 --> 00:12:04.985
Take it away, bro.

00:12:04.985 --> 00:12:07.446
- Duke, thanks so much for the question.

00:12:07.446 --> 00:12:09.902
It's a really good one, and
one that I could probably

00:12:09.902 --> 00:12:11.527
spend a couple of hours talking through,

00:12:11.527 --> 00:12:15.052
but I know this show
is long enough already.

00:12:15.052 --> 00:12:16.677
Tryin' to think through it, like I said,

00:12:16.677 --> 00:12:17.824
there's a lot I could go through.

00:12:17.824 --> 00:12:19.756
I think one of the biggest
things is perspective.

00:12:19.756 --> 00:12:24.284
I think that, in the course of
growing a business very fast,

00:12:24.284 --> 00:12:25.747
there's a lot that gets thrown at you.

00:12:25.747 --> 00:12:27.651
And there's a lot of good,
and there's a lot of bad.

00:12:27.651 --> 00:12:30.298
And it's really keeping
the highs not too high,

00:12:30.298 --> 00:12:31.668
and the lows not too low.

00:12:31.668 --> 00:12:33.270
And really taking a step back,

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.338
thinking about the wider impact

00:12:34.338 --> 00:12:36.103
of everything that's happening and really,

00:12:36.103 --> 00:12:38.007
just not stressing yourself out too much.

00:12:38.007 --> 00:12:40.491
I think every day goes by, a lot happens,

00:12:40.491 --> 00:12:42.418
but you can really just
focus on what's important,

00:12:42.418 --> 00:12:44.225
think about the big picture.

00:12:44.225 --> 00:12:45.680
That's been massively beneficial for me

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.420
as we've grown the business
together at Vayner.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.748
Another huge one for me, is just the value

00:12:51.748 --> 00:12:54.266
of the team and HR.

00:12:54.266 --> 00:12:58.422
And just really focusing on personalizing

00:12:58.422 --> 00:13:00.419
the experience with your staff.

00:13:00.419 --> 00:13:04.273
I think, you know, when focusing on HR,

00:13:04.273 --> 00:13:06.572
I think there's a temptation
to be a little bit

00:13:06.572 --> 00:13:10.774
too by-the-book, you
know follow a process,

00:13:10.774 --> 00:13:13.723
a handbook, of how to handle reviews,

00:13:13.723 --> 00:13:15.883
and how to handle situations,

00:13:15.883 --> 00:13:17.963
and we very much take a
look at every situation

00:13:17.963 --> 00:13:20.609
that comes our way, with
anybody that we work with.

00:13:20.609 --> 00:13:22.137
And really personalize
that, and really think

00:13:22.137 --> 00:13:24.064
about the situation and the impact of it.

00:13:24.064 --> 00:13:26.377
And don't use a cookie cutter system.

00:13:26.377 --> 00:13:28.718
I think just really
focusing on HR, you know,

00:13:28.718 --> 00:13:32.177
we grew very fast at Vayner,
we went through a spurt, of,

00:13:32.177 --> 00:13:35.586
roughly, from 12
employees to 25 employees,

00:13:35.586 --> 00:13:38.535
to 100 to 250 to 400.

00:13:38.535 --> 00:13:39.788
And when you're growing that fast,

00:13:39.788 --> 00:13:41.112
I think the two things
that I've mentioned:

00:13:41.112 --> 00:13:43.633
really keeping perspective
and big-picture thoughts,

00:13:43.633 --> 00:13:47.580
and really making sure that
you're focusing on the team,

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:50.831
and the team within, and
focusing on their growth,

00:13:50.831 --> 00:13:53.594
how they work with you, how
they work with each other,

00:13:53.594 --> 00:13:55.869
and those are the two biggest
things I think I've taken away

00:13:55.869 --> 00:13:58.981
from working with Gary and
having him as my brother,

00:13:58.981 --> 00:14:00.950
my business partner, and my mentor.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.622
And my best friend.

00:14:02.622 --> 00:14:04.168
- 'Preciate it bro, nice answer.

